turretBacklashCPCheckout.scr
turretBacklashCheckout.scr
        CP or MK turret device backlash removal experiment
        - Check the lifter is raised
        - Log the device record velocity and backlash configuration
        - Manually switch on the turret power
        - Make sure the turret begins at position B
        - Move grating turret towards position C - slowly, with no BLCO
        - Move grating turret to position C - normal velocity with BLCO
        - Move grating turret towards position D - slowly, with no BLCO
        - Move grating turret to position D - normal velocity with BLCO
        - Move grating turret towards position A - slowly, with no BLCO
        - Move grating turret to position A - normal velocity with BLCO
        - Move grating turret towards position D - slowly, with no BLCO
        - Move grating turret to position D - normal velocity with negative
          BLCO
        - Move grating turret towards position C - slowly, with no BLCO
        - Move grating turret to position C - normal velocity with negative
          BLCO
        - Move grating turret towards position B - slowly, with no BLCO
        - Move grating turret to position B - normal velocity with negative
          BLCO
        - Restore the BLCO back to normal and reindex
        - Move grating turret back to position B - normal velocity with
          BLCO
        - Finally switch off the turret power

