        - Visual check for positioning accuracy at position B
        - Move grating turret to position C
        - Visual check for positioning accuracy at position C
        - Move grating turret to position D
        - Visual check for positioning accuracy at position D
        - Move grating turret to position A
        - Visual check for positioning accurancy at position A
        - Move grating turret backwards to position D
        - Visual check for positioning accuracy at position D
        - Move grating turret backwards to position C
        - Visual check for positioning accuracy at position C
        - Move grating turret backwards to position B
        - Visual check for positioning accuracy at position B
        - Test long move directly to position A
        - Visual check for positioning accuracy at position A
        - Test long backwards move to position B
        - Visual check for positioning accuracy at position B


turretIndexCheckout.scr
        Index the turret on the lower hard limit switch.
        (Only necessary when the limit switches are broken).

turretJudderCPCheckout.scr
turretJudderCheckout.scr
        Take the CP or MK grating turret device through a series
        of moves to look for juddering. (Only necessary to check
        whether the drive has worn and needs refurbishment).

turretSetupCheckout.scr
        Obsolete setup script?
        (Only necessary when the limit switches are broken).

wheel1Checkout.scr
wheel2Checkout.scr
        Test the filter wheel devices
        - Verify startup state
        - Log the current device record configuration
        - Test filter wheel device INIT mode
        - Test filter wheel device TEST mode
        - Index filter wheel
        - Place filter wheel device in each position in turn
        - Test in-position switche
        - Place filter wheel device in the gaps between two positions in turn
        - Test in-position switches
        - Reindex filter wheel

xaxisCheckout.scr
yaxisCheckout.scr
        Test the detector translation X and Y axis devices
        - Verify startup state
        - Log the current device record configuration
        - Test translation stage device INIT mode
        - Test translation stage device TEST mode
        - Test lower limit switch
        - Test upper limit switch
        - Index translation stage device
        - Deliberately move translation stage device into lower soft limit
        - Index translation stage device from lower limit
        - Deliberately move translation stage device into upper soft limit
        - Index translation stage device from upper limit
        - Request position well below lower software limit and check response
        - Request position well above upper software limit and check response
        - Move translation stage device to park position
        - Verify state and log park position

zaxisCheckout.scr
        Test the detector translation Z axis device
        - Verify startup state
        - Log the current device record configuration
        - Test translation stage Z axis device INIT mode
        - Test translation stage Z axis device TEST mode
        - Test lower limit switch
        - Test upper limit switch
        - Index translation stage Z axis
        - Deliberately move translation stage Z axis into upper soft limit
        - Index translation stage Z axis
        - Request position well below lower software limit and check response
        - Request position well above upper software limit and check response
        - Move translation stage Z axis to park position
        - Verify state and log park position

General purpose checkout scripts
--------------------------------

nullCheckout.scr
        NULL checkout script used for testing higher level shell scripts.


Shell Scripts
-------------

add
        binary (see src directory)
        This Unix program is designed to be called from a C shell script
        when there is a need to add together two or more floating point
        variables. All the arguments supplied to the program on the command
        line are added together and the result written to the standard output.
        Used by: ?

assemblyCommand
        To start an Assembly record command and monitor its progress.
        Used by: cassetteErrCheckout; extractorErrCheckout.

checkAlign
        Check whether mask slot is aligned then advance to next slot.
        Keep checking until no more cassettes are found or an error. 
        Used by: cassettePinCheckout.

checkCommand
        To check a Device record command and monitor for
        acceptance or rejection.
        Used by: cassetteErrCheckout; extractorErrCheckout.

checkState
        To wait for a record to go into a given state.
        Used by: filterCheckout; filterNoUpdateCheckout; gratingCalibCheckout;
        gratingCheckout; gratingNoUpdateCheckout; maskCheckout; maskIcdCheckout; 
        maskUpdateCheckout; translationCheckout; wfsCheckout;
        wfsIcdCheckout; wfsPatrolCheckout.

compareField
        To compare contents of an epics record field with the value of
        another field.
        Used by: cassetteCheckout; extractorCheckout; filterCheckout;
        filterNoUpdateCheckout; gratingCalibCheckout; gratingCheckout;
        gratingNoUpdateCheckout; maskCheckout; maskIcdCheckout;
        maskOptoDelayCheckout; maskOptoSensorCheckout; maskUpdateCheckout;
        translationCheckout.

deviceCommand
        To start a Device record command and monitor its progress.
        Used by: cassetteCheckout; cassetteErrCheckout; cassettePinCheckout; 
        extractorCheckout; extractorErrCheckout; grip Checkout; 
        lifterCheckout; maskCheckout; maskIcdCheckout;
        maskOptoSensorCheckout; releaseCheckout; tiltACheckout;
        tiltBCheckout; tiltCCheckout; tiltDCheckout;
        turretBacklashCPCheckout; turretBacklashCheckout; turretCheckout;
        turretFullCheckout; turretIndexCheckout; turretJudderCPCheckout;
        turretJudderCheckout; turretSetupCheckout; wfsCheckout;
        wheel1Checkout; wheel2Checkout; xaxisCheckout; yzxisCheckout;
        zaxisCheckout.

executeAcquisition
        To start a GMOS observation and wait for the data acquisition 
        to finish.
        Used by: flexLog

executeApplyCommand
        To start a CAD/CAR record command via the "apply" record.
        Used by: instrumentCheckout.

executeCommand
        To start a CAD/CAR record command.
        Used by: detectorCheckout; filterCheckout; filterNoUpdateCheckout;
        gratingCalibCheckout; gratingCheckout; gratingNoUpdateCheckout;
        maskCheckout; maskIcdCheckout; maskOptoDelayCheckout;
        maskOptoSensorCheckout; maskUpdateCheckout; translationCheckout;
        wfsCheckout; wfsIcdCheckout; wfsPatrolCheckout.

executeObserve
        To start a GMOS observation and wait for the whole thing to finish.
        Used by: flexLog; flexLog_sciOnly; crosstalk*; focusLog;  hartAB;
        hartABCD; hartCD; hartFocusRun; logImages;

finishCommand
        To wait for a CAD/CAR command to complete.
        Used by: filterCheckout; filterNoUpdateCheckout; gratingCalibCheckout;
        gratingCheckout; gratingNoUpdateCheckout; maskCheckout; maskIcdCheckout;
        maskUpdateCheckout; translationCheckout; wfsCheckout; 
        wfsIcdCheckout; wfsPatrolCheckout.

getChannel
        To get the value of an EPICS channel and report it to stdout.
        Used by: ?

getFilterId
        To recover a filter ID from the lookup table and 
        load it into the assembly record.
        Used by: filterCheckout; filterNoUpdateCheckout.

getFirstMaskId
        To recover the first mask ID from the lookup table and 
        load it into the assembly record.
        Used by: maskCheckout; maskIcdCheckout.

getGratingId
        To recover a grating ID from the lookup table and 
        load it into the assembly record.
        Used by: gratingCheckout; gratingNoUpdateCheckout.

getLastMaskId
        To recover the last mask ID from the lookup table and 
        load it into the assembly record.
        Used by: maskCheckout; maskIcdCheckout; maskOptoSensorCheckout.

getMaskId
        To recover a mask ID from the lookup table and 
        load it into the assembly record.
        Used by: maskUpdateCheckout

getMaskNum
        To recover number of masks in mask lookup table.
        Used by: ?

lifterExhaust
        To activate the lifter exhaust for a few seconds.
        This primitive may be used to guard against leaks
        into the grating lifter while running a checkout
        script.
        Used by: (An option for gratingJuggle and logImages)

lifterRaise
        To activate the lifter raise for a few seconds.
        This primitive may be used to guard against leaks
        in the grating lifter that might cause the lifter to
        drift downwards while running a checkout script.
        Used by: (An option for gratingJuggle and logImages)

moveAssembly
        To configure a GMOS assembly.
        Used by: flexLog; flexLog_sciOnly; crosstalk*; focusLog; hartAB;
        hartABCD; hartCD; hartFocusRun; logImages;

moveCommand
        To request a move of a Device record. It will check the
        acknowledgement of the command and wait until the BUSY
        line goes to IDLE or ERR.  It will then check the
        MPOS matches the requested position and that the
        current motor is STOPPED.  It will also check that
        the home position is valid.
        If a last argument is given, then this is a move to
        a named position.
        Used by: ?

mult
        binary (see src directory)
        This Unix program is designed to be called from a C shell script
        when there is a need to multiply together two or more floating point
        variables. All the arguments supplied to the program on the command
        line are multiplied together and the result written to the standard 
        output.
        Used by: gratingJuggle; logImages; logTemps; turretSimUpdate;
        turretSimupdateSim.

presetCommand
        To preset an Assembly record command and monitor for
        acceptance or rejection.
        Used by: filterCheckout; filterNoUpdateCheckout; gratingCheckout;
        gratingNoUpdateCheckout; maskIcdCheckout; translationCheckout;
        wfsIcdCheckout.

rand
        binary (see src directory)
        Generate a seeded random integer between 0 and N-1.
        This Unix program is designed to be called from a C shell script.
        Used by: instrumentConfigCheckout

setField
        To load an epics record field with the value of another field.
        Used by: cassetteErrCheckout; extractorErrCheckout; maskCheckout;
        wfsCheckout; wfsIcdCheckout.

setObserveFilename
        To set the file name for a GMOS observation.
        Used by: flexLog; flexLog_sciOnly; crosstalk*; focusLog; hartAB;
        hartABCD; hartCD; hartFocusRun; logImages;

setObserveROI
        To set the file name for a GMOS observation.
        Used by: flexLog; flexLog_sciOnly;

setWfsFilename
        To set the file name for a GMOS wavefront sensor observation.
        Used by: flexLog; flexLog_sciOnly; wfsImageLog;

startCommand
        To start a CAD/CAR record command.
        Used by: filterCheckout; filterNoUpdateCheckout; gratingCalibCheckout;
        gratingCheckout; gratingNoUpdateCheckout; maskCheckout; maskIcdCheckout;
        maskUpdateCheckout; translationCheckout; wfsCheckout;
        wfsIcdCheckout; wfsPatrolCheckout.

stopCommand
        To stop a CAD/CAR command.
        Used by: maskIcdCheckout.

tolower
        binary (see src directory)
        Convert all characters to lower case. Accept string(s).  This 
        Unix program is designed to be called from a C shell script.
        Used by: flexLog; flexLog_sciOnly; focusLog; hartAB;
        hartABCD; hartCD; hartFocusRun.

wfsObserve
        To start a GMOS WFS observation.
        Used by: flexLog; flexLog_sciOnly; wfsImageLog;
